cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Replication package for "Latency optimization and oracle-based failure
  diagnosis in interactive adaptive learning pipelines"
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite both the accompanying
  article and this archive.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Bertalan
    family-names: Forstner
    email: bertalan.forstner@aut.bme.hu
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Automation and Applied Informatics, Faculty of Electrical
      Engineering and Informatics, Budapest University of Technology and
      Economics
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # TODO: add before release
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation, benchmark harness and complete measurement scripts
  for an oracle-localised measurement study of the recommendation critical path
  of Coglica, a research platform for game-based cognitive assessment. The
  package reproduces every table and figure in the article: the oracle
  substitution that localises the lost value to the predictor, the sweep of the
  two interacting configuration choices inside it, the latency decomposition and
  the four-runtime cost model, the closed-form enumeration/search crossover, the
  search-strategy comparison, the concurrency sweep and the degradation chain
  measured in the domain metric.
keywords:
  - adaptive learning
  - machine learning systems engineering
  - inference latency
  - graceful degradation
  - oracle analysis
  - declarative configuration
  - reproducibility
